# ClangSharp configuration for src/Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.Native/Generated/.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING. This rsp deviates from the house style in three
# places, and every one of them was forced by a measured failure rather than
# chosen. The comment blocks below say which. In particular: do not "restore"
# strip-enum-member-type-name for consistency with the other rsps, and do not
# drop generate-macro-bindings as an optimisation.
#
# The parse root is OUR header, not NVIDIA's. native/ngx/src/ahjo_ngx.h
# includes <vulkan/vulkan.h> and then nvsdk_ngx_vk.h (the NGX headers do not
# include Vulkan themselves, verified at nvsdk_ngx_vk.h:69-77), and declares
# the AhjoNgxInitInfo UTF-8 mirror plus the seven ahjo_ngx_* entry points. It
# is both the shim's header and this file's parse root, so there is exactly
# one definition of the mirror struct and no cross-language layout agreement
# to maintain.
--file
native/ngx/src/ahjo_ngx.h
# --traverse is the COMPLETE set, not an addition to --file: leave ahjo_ngx.h
# off this list and our own declarations vanish from the output.
#
# Traversal alone excludes the entire D3D11/D3D12/CUDA *entry-point* surface,
# because those live in nvsdk_ngx.h and the dlssd/dlssg headers, which are not
# listed here. Measured; no --exclude is needed for them.
--traverse
native/ngx/src/ahjo_ngx.h
native/ngx/include/nvsdk_ngx_vk.h
native/ngx/include/nvsdk_ngx_defs.h
native/ngx/include/nvsdk_ngx_defs_vk.h
native/ngx/include/nvsdk_ngx_params.h
--include-directory
native/ngx/stubs
--include-directory
native/stubs
--include-directory
native/include
--include-directory
native/ngx/include
--namespace
Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.Native
# NOT "Ngx": a type named Ngx inside namespace Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.Native would be
# unreachable from namespace Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx, because the identifier binds to
# the enclosing namespace before any imported type. That is the #166 lesson,
# recorded at tools/generate-slang.rsp:19-21.
--methodClassName
NgxApi
# The shim, not the NGX client library: NVIDIA ships a static archive with no
# DLL to P/Invoke, so all 27 entry points resolve against ahjo_ngx.dll /
# libahjo_ngx.so. native/ngx/src/ahjo_ngx.def and .map are the export lists.
--libraryPath
ahjo_ngx
--output
src/Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.Native/Generated
--output-mode
CSharp
# C, not C++. NVSDK_NGX_Parameter is a C++ abstract class with nine pure
# virtuals (nvsdk_ngx_params.h:53-76); binding its vtable would be both wrong
# (the driver produces the object, not us) and unstable. The 16 exported
# NVSDK_NGX_Parameter_{Set,Get}* C accessors are the SDK's own supported C
# path and are real defined symbols in both static libraries, verified with
# llvm-nm --defined-only.
--language
c
# Same reproducibility argument as tools/generate-ktx.rsp:30-38: pin the parse
# target so generated output is a function of NgxVersion alone.
#
# It matters more here than anywhere else in this repo, because wchar_t is
# 2 bytes on Windows and 4 on Linux. Under this fixed target a wchar_t* comes
# out as int* — a UTF-32 buffer — which Windows would then read as UTF-16.
# That is why the wide-string structs are excluded below and the shim exposes
# UTF-8 mirrors instead. Nothing wide may ever appear in Generated/; if a
# regen introduces one, exclude the struct. Do NOT --remap wchar_t: that makes
# Windows right and Linux wrong, which is a per-RID lie in a file whose whole
# purpose is being host-independent.
--additional
--target=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
--config
latest-codegen
generate-helper-types
generate-file-scoped-namespaces
# DELTA 1 — generate-macro-bindings, which no other rsp in this repo turns on.
#
# nvsdk_ngx_defs.h defines 204 NVSDK_NGX_Parameter_* string macros ("Width",
# "Color", "Jitter.Offset.X", "DLSS.Hint.Render.Preset.DLAA", …). With
# generate-unmanaged-constants alone, ZERO of them are emitted — measured, by
# grepping the generated tree for "Width" and matching only struct fields.
# With this flag they come out as
#
#     public static ReadOnlySpan<byte> NVSDK_NGX_Parameter_Width => "Width"u8;
#
# i.e. exactly the UTF-8 literal form the repo's invariant 1 requires, in
# read-only data, allocating nothing per frame. Without this flag the
# parameter names would have to be hand-written, which is the drift this whole
# project exists to avoid.
#
# The cost is DELTA 3 below: it also emits the legacy hash-encoded alias
# family, which has to be excluded.
generate-macro-bindings
generate-unmanaged-constants
generate-disable-runtime-marshalling
generate-aggressive-inlining
exclude-enum-operators
# DELTA 2 — strip-enum-member-type-name is ABSENT, and must stay absent.
#
# All three other rsps use it. Here it does not compile. NVSDK_NGX_Result is a
# bitwise-or chain off one member (nvsdk_ngx_defs.h:96-178):
#
#     NVSDK_NGX_Result_Fail = 0xBAD00000,
#     NVSDK_NGX_Result_FAIL_FeatureNotSupported = NVSDK_NGX_Result_Fail | 1,
#
# The stripper rewrites member NAMES but not initializer expressions that
# reference sibling members, so the second line generates as
# `FAIL_FeatureNotSupported = NVSDK_NGX_Result_Fail | 1` — 18 x CS0103.
# Measured. Dropping the flag fixes all 18 and the output builds with 0
# warnings and 0 errors under TreatWarningsAsErrors + AnalysisLevel=latest.
#
# The consequence is that enum members keep their NVSDK_NGX_-prefixed names in
# this one project. That is deliberate; do not "fix" it.
multi-file
--remap
size_t=nuint
# Ten Vk* remaps into Ahjo.Vulkan.Native, the tools/generate-vma.rsp pattern.
# This is what makes Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.Native a genuine Vulkan consumer and why
# it ProjectReferences Ahjo.Vulkan.Native, unlike the Slang and KTX packages.
VkInstance_T=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkInstance_T
VkPhysicalDevice_T=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkPhysicalDevice_T
VkDevice_T=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkDevice_T
VkCommandBuffer_T=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkCommandBuffer_T
VkImage_T=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkImage_T
VkImageView_T=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkImageView_T
VkBuffer_T=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkBuffer_T
VkFormat=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkFormat
VkImageSubresourceRange=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkImageSubresourceRange
VkExtensionProperties=Ahjo.Vulkan.Native.VkExtensionProperties
--exclude
# GROUP 1 — the wide-string structs, and the two that exist only to be
# embedded in them. Excluding the wchar_t-taking FUNCTIONS is not enough:
# NVSDK_NGX_PathListInfo.Path would still be generated as int** and
# NVSDK_NGX_FeatureDiscoveryInfo.ApplicationDataPath as int*, leaving a public
# surface a caller could fill with Encoding.UTF32 and ship a Windows-only bug.
# AhjoNgxInitInfo in native/ngx/src/ahjo_ngx.h is their UTF-8 replacement.
NVSDK_NGX_PathListInfo
NVSDK_NGX_LoggingInfo
NVSDK_NGX_FeatureCommonInfo
NVSDK_NGX_FeatureCommonInfo_Internal
NVSDK_NGX_FeatureDiscoveryInfo
NVSDK_NGX_ProjectIdDescription
NVSDK_NGX_Application_Identifier
# GROUP 2 — entry points the shim does not export, so a binding for them could
# only ever produce an EntryPointNotFoundException. Same reasoning as
# tools/generate-ktx.rsp:61-68.
#
# The four Init/discovery calls are replaced by ahjo_ngx_*_utf8 equivalents
# (they take wchar_t). GetNGXResultAsString returns const wchar_t* and is
# replaced by ahjo_ngx_result_to_utf8. RequiredExtensions is deprecated by its
# own header comment (nvsdk_ngx_vk.h:83-86) in favour of the two discovery
# calls, and CreateFeature is superseded by CreateFeature1, the multi-device
# form.
NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_Init
NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_Init_with_ProjectID
NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_GetFeatureRequirements
NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_GetFeatureInstanceExtensionRequirements
NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_GetFeatureDeviceExtensionRequirements
GetNGXResultAsString
NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_RequiredExtensions
NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_CreateFeature
# GROUP 3 — the D3D parameter accessors. Their 12 siblings ship; these four
# take ID3D11Resource / ID3D12Resource, which this package has no business
# naming.
NVSDK_NGX_Parameter_SetD3d11Resource
NVSDK_NGX_Parameter_SetD3d12Resource
NVSDK_NGX_Parameter_GetD3d11Resource
NVSDK_NGX_Parameter_GetD3d12Resource
# GROUP 4 — foreign-API opaque declarations the headers forward-declare
# (nvsdk_ngx_defs.h:555-562, nvsdk_ngx_params.h). They are never defined, so
# there is nothing to emit and the references dangle.
IUnknown
ID3D11Resource
ID3D11Buffer
ID3D11Texture2D
ID3D12Resource
D3D11_TEXTURE2D_DESC
D3D11_BUFFER_DESC
D3D12_RESOURCE_DESC
CD3DX12_HEAP_PROPERTIES
NVSDK_NGX_CUDADevice
NVSDK_NGX_DLDenoise_Create_Params
# DELTA 3 / GROUP 5 — the 74 NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_* macros that DELTA 1 would
# otherwise emit.
#
# These are the deprecated hash-encoded aliases of the string names above:
#
#     #define NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Width  "#\x10"    // nvsdk_ngx_defs.h:588
#
# ClangSharp escapes \t, \n, \r and \0 but emits 0x01-0x08, 0x0b, 0x0c and
# 0x0e-0x1f LITERALLY — a byte histogram of the generated NgxApi.cs found 28
# distinct raw control bytes in the file. Nothing in the DLSS path uses them,
# and committing raw control characters into a *.cs file that .gitattributes:2
# puts under text=auto eol=lf normalization is a hazard with no upside.
#
# Regenerate this list mechanically after a pin bump rather than hand-editing
# it. The one-liner is in src/Ahjo.Vulkan.Ngx.Native/CLAUDE.md.
#
# GROUP 6 — the three function-like macros DELTA 1 also trips over.
# NVSDK_NGX_ARRAY_LEN (nvsdk_ngx_defs.h:48), NVSDK_NGX_SUCCEED (:183) and
# NVSDK_NGX_FAILED (:184) take arguments, and generate-macro-bindings cannot
# express that, so each produces
#
#     Warning: Function like macro definition records are not supported
#
# ClangSharpPInvokeGenerator exits with its DIAGNOSTIC COUNT, so those three
# warnings are an exit code of 3 and MSBuild's Exec fails the Regenerate
# target even though the output is complete and correct. Excluding them is
# both the fix and the right answer on merit: they are C convenience macros
# (`sizeof(a)/sizeof(a[0])`, and two result-code predicates), none of which
# has a meaningful C# form. Verified: with these three excluded the generator
# exits 0.
NVSDK_NGX_ARRAY_LEN
NVSDK_NGX_SUCCEED
NVSDK_NGX_FAILED
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Reserved00
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_SuperSampling_Available
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_InPainting_Available
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_ImageSuperResolution_Available
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_SlowMotion_Available
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_VideoSuperResolution_Available
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Reserved06
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Reserved07
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Reserved08
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_ImageSignalProcessing_Available
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_ImageSuperResolution_ScaleFactor_2_1
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_ImageSuperResolution_ScaleFactor_3_1
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_ImageSuperResolution_ScaleFactor_3_2
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_ImageSuperResolution_ScaleFactor_4_3
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_NumFrames
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Scale
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Width
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Height
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_OutWidth
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_OutHeight
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Sharpness
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Scratch
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Scratch_SizeInBytes
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_EvaluationNode
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Input1
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Input1_Format
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Input1_SizeInBytes
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Input2
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Input2_Format
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Input2_SizeInBytes
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Color
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Color_Format
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Color_SizeInBytes
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Albedo
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Output
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Output_Format
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Output_SizeInBytes
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Reset
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_BlendFactor
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_MotionVectors
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Rect_X
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Rect_Y
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Rect_W
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Rect_H
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_MV_Scale_X
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_MV_Scale_Y
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Model
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Format
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_SizeInBytes
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_ResourceAllocCallback
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_BufferAllocCallback
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Tex2DAllocCallback
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_ResourceReleaseCallback
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_CreationNodeMask
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_VisibilityNodeMask
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_PreviousOutput
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_MV_Offset_X
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_MV_Offset_Y
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Hint_UseFireflySwatter
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Resource_Width
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Resource_Height
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Depth
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_DLSSOptimalSettingsCallback
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_PerfQualityValue
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_RTXValue
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_DLSSMode
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_DeepResolve_Available
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_Deprecated_43
NVSDK_NGX_EParameter_OptLevel
